{"copyright":{"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20240014551,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"containsIndication":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"2244a56dd26243da9ce61737b45e9e75","belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Spacecraft Design, Testing and Performance"],"keywords":["methodology","evaluation","fire risk","electrical","faults","oxygen","environments"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20240014551,"ear":"NO","id":"47ba8bc2d734412a86a44e9f73c264d9","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2024-11-18T07:00:00.0000000+00:00","fundingNumbers":[{"number":"80JSC022DA003","submissionId":20240014551,"id":"181031703ca844c783b69b88c4bbbcfa","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"}],"title":"A New Test Methodology for Evaluating Fire Risk Due to Electrical Faults in Oxygen-Enriched Environments","stiType":"ABSTRACT","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2024-11-15T22:40:07.7056970+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"organizationId":"51d92752487149f08037942e2302fbf7","sequence":0,"submissionId":20240014551,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Stephen F Peralta"},"organization":{"name":"White Sands Test Facility","location":"Las Cruces, United States"}},"id":"0de7899d7117444aa4fd8d40d6ab4077","userType":"CIVIL","userId":"7e9e7d62b08c49409d9ffbbe0617367f"},{"organizationId":"49d5185d6d735ca7863b63184bc72700","sequence":1,"submissionId":20240014551,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Timothy D Gallus"},"organization":{"name":"Sierra Lobo (United States)","location":"Fremont, Ohio, United States"}},"id":"10691d01582d45749ad9158f3a62454a","userType":"CONTRACTOR_GRANTEE","userId":"6a8538ae6f574713860becfddb695ec1"},{"organizationId":"68603dff261e5d2d9de5a550aa9e6b30","sequence":2,"submissionId":20240014551,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Gregory J Harrigan"},"organization":{"name":"Langley Research Center","location":"Hampton, United States"}},"id":"68b372a8d7664ed6a24e7a1bcafe1a9d","userType":"CIVIL","userId":"c5459eab037b4e49a8edb17e67763c35"},{"organizationId":"5a078aec66f45971ad414409688d6379","sequence":3,"submissionId":20240014551,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Thomas K Evans"},"organization":{"name":"Millennium Engineering and Integration (United States)","location":"Arlington, Virginia, United States"}},"id":"7d93ad5f133f4253bee0e1eb3af42e36","userType":"CONTRACTOR_GRANTEE","userId":"02436adb7b4a458e8b73069353732651"},{"organizationId":"49d5185d6d735ca7863b63184bc72700","sequence":4,"submissionId":20240014551,"meta":{"author":{"name":"DeAngelo D Maestas"},"organization":{"name":"Sierra Lobo (United States)","location":"Fremont, Ohio, United States"}},"id":"75e65139718f4cb68c1b689e23db87f9","userType":"OTHER","userId":"ad5d51ec3c064deda5b4c595ec013a49"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Abstract","technicalReviewType":"NASA_PEER_COMMITTEE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20240014551,"created":"2024-11-15T17:43:00.9409490+00:00","center":{"code":"JSC","name":"Johnson Space Center","id":"dd46994b91a94cb2a2722617cbbadc55"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"This paper discusses a new test methodology for assessing the safe use of materials found in spacecraft that may be exposed to electrical faults, as performed at the NASA White Sands Test Facility. “Wire-break” testing, modeled after the Cleveland Open Cup method, identifies the conditions under which pyrolyzed material transitions from a brief flash to a propagating flame. The approach focuses on fuel mass liberated through pyrolysis, mixed with oxygen, and ignited by a piloted ignition (spark due to fusion of wire) to achieve flame propagation with the least energy. The test approach attempts to find energy density thresholds derived using I²t values from current-induced heating of various test materials and wire characteristics. The application of the data provides a useful approach to mitigating fire risks in space systems by correlating threshold data to real-world designs and scaling factors, including oxygen pressure, wire diameter, heat sinking, and contained smoke volume. Several case studies, including Apollo missions and hypothetical scenarios, illustrate practical applications of these thresholds to enhance fire safety design considerations in space environments.","isLessonsLearned":true,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","cui":{"isCui":false,"submissionId":20240014551,"id":"43f2f441c3834d9b897b45f5dce73919"},"meetings":[{"country":"CZ","submissionId":20240014551,"endDate":"2025-07-17T06:00:00.0000000+00:00","sponsors":[{"organizationId":"a4c6a63ed02340b68240e18a1c0d30ce","meta":{"organization":{"name":"International Conference on Environmental Systems (ICES) ","location":""}},"meetingId":"68759edc34bd44d29332111d6467c46e","id":"9698df397ee14e8fa7d4545e083a180b"}],"name":"54th International Conference on Environmental Systems","location":"Prague","id":"68759edc34bd44d29332111d6467c46e","url":"https://ices.space/###","startDate":"2025-07-13T06:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"20220003562.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20240014551/downloads/20220003562.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20240014551/downloads/20220003562.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20240014551/downloads/20220003562.pdf.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"}